ing tests were relocated, not dropped.\n\n**`cli.ts` semantics (task 4) — clean.** `--kind` stays a plain string from the CLI arg parser (`Flags` is `{[key]: string|boolean}`, never an array), so the `ReadOptions.kind: string|string[]` widening in `annals` doesn't change CLI behavior; the `typeof opts.kind === \"string\"` guard in `displayFilter` is equivalent to the old `opts.kind !== undefined` check for every real CLI call. `readOptionsFrom`'s `--conversation` flag correctly now sets `opts.stream`. `loadConfig(repo)` (was `loadConfig(repo.root)`) matches the new `redact/config.ts` wrapper signature at both call sites (`cmdScan`, `cmdReAnchor`). Command dispatch (`append/log/show/conversations/export/sync/transport-push/scan/review/inspect/allow/redact/re-anchor/renormalize/install/hook/capture`) is structurally untouched and all imports resolve. Verified empirically: `tsc --noEmit` is clean and `node --test dist/test/**/*.test.js` passes 90/90.\n\n**Schema version change — real but intentional, documented.** `SCHEMA_VERSION` changed from `\"conversation-ledger/v1\"` to `\"annals/v1\"` (in `annals/src/schema.ts`). This is not part of the mechanical rename and is a genuine behavior change: every newly captured event now carries a different `schema` string than the pre-refactor history. It does **not** break reading old events — `validateEvent`'s schema check only runs inside `finalizeEvent` (write path), never on `parseEventLine` (read path) — so old notes remain readable. It's explicitly acknowledged as \"wipe, not migrate\" in `README.md`'s new paragraph and in `scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh`'s rationale comment. Severity: known-tradeoff, already surfaced by the author's own tooling.\n\n**Packaging (task 6) — real bug, but likely known WIP.** `package.json` adds `\"dependencies\": { \"annals\": \"file:../annals\" }`. Verified empirically with `npm pack`: the tarball's `package.json` retains `\"annals\": \"file:../annals\"` verbatim, and annals' `dist/` is **not** bundled into the tarball (only cledger's own 84 files). If this were published to npm today, `npm install -g conversation-ledger` (or any install off the registry) on a machine without an identical `~/repos/evintunador/annals` sibling checkout would fail to resolve the `annals` dependency at install time — the package is currently unpublishable/uninstallable outside the author's own monorepo layout. Not caused by the rename work per se, but a direct consequence of this refactor and worth flagging before any `npm publish`. `bin`/`files`/`dist/cli.js` chmod are otherwise unchanged and correct. Severity: real bug (packaging), but consistent with a deliberately unpushed, in-progress branch (per commit `78c9f8c`: \"0.26.0: sit on annals\").\n\n**No dropped features found.** Every function, type, and constant that was part of `main`'s actual public surface (`src/index.ts`) is present and behaviorally identical on `annals-extraction`. The things that did shrink (a few internal helper re-exports in `git.ts`/`review.ts`/`store.ts`) were never on that public surface and have no remaining callers in `src/`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>112293</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>79</tool_uses><duration_ms>369846</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0d114-c718-71e0-8068-515b8a2d04ca","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4eba8fc0bc16e916</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Ak1xrDcxzTJKq8NFrRinpZ</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/70d37a6f-cede-498c-b2df-0b0a320db72a/tasks/a4eba8fc0bc16e916.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit annals vs old store layer\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Audit Report: conversation-ledger → annals extraction\n\n**Method:** diffed all 15 named files (`git show main:src/X` vs `annals/src/X`), read every hunk, cross-checked every export symbol against `annals/src/index.ts`, and grepped `annals/src` for residual `cledger`/`conversation-ledger`/`ev1-`/`conversation-ledger/v1` literals.\n\n**Files byte-identical to `main` (no findings):** `git.ts`, `canonical.ts`, `redact/apply.ts`, `forge/forge.ts`, `forge/github.ts`, `reanchor-suggest.ts`.\n\n**Files with only intended, mechanical changes:** `schema.ts` (SCHEMA_VERSION, `ev1-`→`ev2-`, `ConversationRef`→`StreamRef`, `KNOWN_KINDS`/`SESSION_MACHINERY_KINDS` cleanly removed with no dangling refs anywhere in annals/src — confirmed matches item 6), `redact/rules.ts` (only `RULESET_VERSION` string changed), `reanchor.ts` (only `producer.tool` changed), `redact/known-secrets.ts`, most of `store.ts`/`transport.ts`/`redact/config.ts`/`redact/scan.ts` (RepoInfo→Ledger, hardcoded ref/dir names → `repo.ns.*`, `ReadOptions.tool`/`kind[]`/`linkRel`, `conversation`→`stream`).\n\n### Real bugs\n\n1. **`store.ts:749`, `remoteNoteIds()`** — temp ref name still hardcoded to `\"conversation-ledger-scan-tmp\"` (should be namespaced like the sibling `pushScopedNotes` tmp ref, which correctly became `` `${repo.ns.name}-push-tmp` `` at line 705). Two `Ledger`s in different namespaces running a scan gate against the same repo would collide on `refs/notes/conversation-ledger-scan-tmp`. **Real bug**, latent (only bites multi-namespace use), matches audit item (b).\n\n2. **`store.ts:766`, `ScanBlockedError`** — old message was `` `cledger sync: push blocked — ...` ``; new is `` `sync: push blocked — ...` `` — the CLI-name prefix wasn't namespaced, it was **dropped entirely** (the constructor takes only `findings: number`, no `cliName`). **Real bug.**\n\n3. **`review.ts:344` and `:350`** — two hardcoded `\"cledger\"` strings survived even though `repo: Ledger` (with `repo.ns.cliName`) is in scope in the enclosing closure:\n   - `\"...event rewritten?) — use cledger redact by hand\"` (should interpolate `repo.ns.cliName`)\n   - `reason: \"cledger review\"` passed into `redactEvent()` — this isn't just a console message, it's **persisted into the redaction event's content** as provenance, so under the default (now \"annals\") or any custom namespace, the ledger permanently records the wrong tool name for who redacted it. **Real bug**, more serious than #2 because it's stored data, not transient output.\n\n4. **`redact/config.ts:99,106`, `readJsonConfig()`** — both `process.stderr.write` warnings hardcode `` `cledger: ignoring ${path}...` ``. `loadConfig(repo: Ledger)` has `repo.ns.cliName` available but doesn't thread it into `readJsonConfig(path: string)`. **Real bug** for non-default namespaces (and prints stale text even in the default case).\n\n### Cosmetic\n\n5. **`redact/scan.ts`, `renderFinding()`** — every other field label in this block is padded to a 13-char column (`rule:        `, `fingerprint: `, `event:       `, `occurred_at: `, `location:    `, `match:       `); the old `conversation:` label was itself exactly 13 chars, keeping the report aligned. New `` `stream:${f.stream ?? \" -\"}` `` is only 7 chars, breaking column alignment in the human-facing `inspect`/`review` report. **Cosmetic.**\n\n6. **`review.ts:159`** — fallback text `${f.stream ?? \"(no conversation)\"}` wasn't updated to say \"(no stream)\" after the field rename. **Cosmetic.**\n\n### Intended, worth knowing\n\n7. `transport.ts hookBlock()` — for the single-hook-block case (the only one that existed pre-extraction) semantics are byte-for-byte preserved: same stdin-once `$(cat)`, same guard-var gate (now namespaced via `internalEnvVar`), same exact-install→PATH fallback chain, same `|| exit $?`. Namespace parametrization now lets multiple independent hook blocks (one per namespace) be chained in one `pre-push` script. That surfaces a new failure mode not present before: the internal capture variable `_annals_refs` isn't namespaced, and since pre-push stdin can only be read once, a second chained block (for a different namespace) will call `$(cat)` on already-drained stdin and silently get an empty ref list. Not a regression for single-namespace use and not explicitly in the 7 intended-change list, but worth flagging as a gap in the new multi-namespace capability.\n\n### Export audit (item a)\n\nEvery exported symbol from all 15 old files is present in `annals/src/index.ts`, except: `NOTES_NAME`/`NOTES_REF`/`INCOMING_NAME`/`INCOMING_REF` → replaced by `notesRef()`/`incomingRef()` functions over `NamespaceConfig` (intended, item 2); `KNOWN_KINDS`/`SESSION_MACHINERY_KINDS` → deliberately dropped (intended, item 6, cledger's own copy is a future concern, not part of this extraction). `git.ts`'s `GitRunOptions`/`statusPorcelain`/`revList` and `forge/github.ts`'s `isGitHubOrigin`/`githubDriver` are absent from `index.ts` in **both** old and new — pre-existing, not a regression.\n\n### Grep audit (item d)\n\nNo `\"ev1-\"` or `\"conversation-ledger/v1\"` literals anywhere in `annals/src`. Remaining `\"cledger\"`/`\"conversation-ledger\"` hits are all comments except the four real bugs listed above (items 1–4).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>117968</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>392790</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0d114-c718-71e0-8068-51684994714f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["unknown"]},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"- are any of the items in the envelope holdovers from cledger's assumptions and instead belonging in content or something rather than as first-class envelope keys?\n- do/should we have any way to enforce the size policy? or maybe out-of-scope for now?\n- what are the other uses that git-bug had of their similar system?\n- d