t is the actual envelope field (`EventDraft.conversation`→`.stream`). Local variables/helpers that happen to be named `conversation` (`conversationFor()`, `conversation.id`, `conversationId` in `records.ts`/`drift.ts`/adapter interfaces) were correctly left alone — none are raw source-JSON keys, none got mis-renamed. `install.ts` wasn't touched by the diff at all and still imports only `hasAuthorIdentity` from `transport.js`, which the wrapper still exports. No leftover `ev1-`, `conversation-ledger/v1`, or stray `.conversation`/`conversation: {}` in `src/` (the one surviving `ev1-` is an intentional comment in `scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh`). Severity: clean.\n\n**`src/index.ts` (task 2) — clean, cosmetic reorg only.** Single diff hunk: `INCOMING_REF`/`NOTES_NAME`/`NOTES_REF` moved from being re-exported via `transport.js` to `store.js`. Values are identical (`store.ts` now defines them directly off `CLEDGER_NAMESPACE`/`A.notesRef`/`A.incomingRef`), so no consumer-visible change. Severity: cosmetic.\n\n**Wrapper completeness (task 3) — clean for the public surface; minor internal shrinkage, unused.**\n- `src/store.ts` no longer re-exports `ensureMergeConfig` (main did, via `transport.js`). It's still exported from `src/transport.ts`. Nothing in `src/` imports it from `store.js`, and `index.ts` never exposed it on main either. Severity: cosmetic.\n- `src/git.ts` drops `statusPorcelain`, `revList`, `GitRunOptions` (unused anywhere in current `src/`, not part of main's `index.ts` surface, still present in `annals/src/git.ts`). Severity: cosmetic.\n- `src/review.ts` drops `Screen`, `ViewState`, `renderView` (unused in `src/`, not on main's public surface). Severity: cosmetic.\n- `src/forge/github.ts` deleted entirely (`isGitHubOrigin`, `githubDriver`); logic now lives in `annals/src/forge/`, `forgeForRepo` still delegates correctly. Severity: clean.\n- `canonical.ts`, `reanchor.ts`, `reanchor-suggest.ts`, `schema.ts`, `redact/apply.ts`, `redact/scan.ts`, `redact/known-secrets.ts`, `redact/config.ts` — export sets verified line-by-line against `main`; all match (modulo the intentional `CledgerConfig = AnnalsConfig` alias). Severity: clean.\n- All ~19 deleted test files have equivalents under `annals/src/test/`, confirming tests were relocated, not dropped.\n\n**`cli.ts` semantics (task 4) — clean.** `--kind` stays a plain string from the CLI arg parser (`Flags` is `{[key]: string|boolean}`, never an array), so the `ReadOptions.kind: string|string[]` widening in `annals` doesn't change CLI behavior; the `typeof opts.kind === \"string\"` guard in `displayFilter` is equivalent to the old `opts.kind !== undefined` check for every real CLI call. `readOptionsFrom`'s `--conversation` flag correctly now sets `opts.stream`. `loadConfig(repo)` (was `loadConfig(repo.root)`) matches the new `redact/config.ts` wrapper signature at both call sites (`cmdScan`, `cmdReAnchor`). Command dispatch (`append/log/show/conversations/export/sync/transport-push/scan/review/inspect/allow/redact/re-anchor/renormalize/install/hook/capture`) is structurally untouched and all imports resolve. Verified empirically: `tsc --noEmit` is clean and `node --test dist/test/**/*.test.js` passes 90/90.\n\n**Schema version change — real but intentional, documented.** `SCHEMA_VERSION` changed from `\"conversation-ledger/v1\"` to `\"annals/v1\"` (in `annals/src/schema.ts`). This is not part of the mechanical rename and is a genuine behavior change: every newly captured event now carries a different `schema` string than the pre-refactor history. It does **not** break reading old events — `validateEvent`'s schema check only runs inside `finalizeEvent` (write path), never on `parseEventLine` (read path) — so old notes remain readable. It's explicitly acknowledged as \"wipe, not migrate\" in `README.md`'s new paragraph and in `scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh`'s rationale comment. Severity: known-tradeoff, already surfaced by the author's own tooling.\n\n**Packaging (task 6) — real bug